Application for variation of condition no. 2 (approved plans) of planning permission dated 28/09/2011, ref: PA/10/01734. Amendments proposed:

Redesign of the Blocks C and L to increase the quantum of business floorspace (Class B1a) from 4,300 sqm to 4,985 sqm (GIA) over two additional storeys; 
Reconfiguration of the basement layout which reduces the quantum of car parking in Phase 4, provides enhanced cycle parking facilities for the employment use and provides adequate space for plant; 
Minor changes to the window positions of residential units in Block K.

Details of all reserved matters (Access, Appearance, Landscaping, Layout and Scale) pursuant to outline planning permission ref PA/13/02966 dated 24/12/2014 relating to the following areas of the Wood Wharf Masterplan:

i. Development Plot G3; 
ii. Ground and above ground infrastructure, streets, landscaping and public realm within Development Zone G; 
iii. Below ground floorspace and infrastructure for Development Plot G3; and 
iv. Ground and above ground infrastructure, streets, landscaping and public realm outside Development Zone G but linked to i, ii and iii above. 

Comprising 176 residential units (Use Class C3), 620sqm of flexible retail, office, leisure and/or community uses (Use Class A1-A5, B1, D1 and D2), ancillary space for circulation and residential facilities; as well as associated infrastructure, streets, landscaping, public realm, parking, servicing and utilities and other associated works.

Application for variation of condition to Planning Permission ref:  PA/13/02162, dated 29/11/2013.

The proposed changes consist of: 
- General internal floor layout amendments to accommodate traditional hotel rooms rather than 'serviced apartments', resulting in an increase in total rooms from 217 to 280 (uplift of 63 rooms); 
- Revised elevations update to reflect the revised internal layout, particularly window locations, and a change in external materials; 
- Provision of substation and relocation of storage areas to rear service yard (as approved under permission PA/16/00970 to refurbish and extend the existing office building); 
- Rationalisation and relocation of plant from basement to rooftop, including the provision of plant screen; 
- Basement layout amendments to accommodate additional front of house accommodation; and 
- Minor basement extension within approved rear light well.

Minor material amendment to condition no.2 of Planning Permission ref: PA/17/03191, Dated 01/03/2018 involving:

- Insertion of a mezzanine to provide an additional 289 sq.m of Class B1 floorspace;
- Lowering part of the ground floor by approx 1.5m to facilitate mezzanine;
- Amendment to cycle storage;
- Rationalisation of core arrangement;
- Residential lift realignment;
- Existing residential side windows replaced with modern versions to match those approved at third and fourth floors.

